integrate computational and statistical methodologies to formulate, model, analyze and solve research problems of interest in a wide variety of applied and theoretical contexts.\nThe data science specialization emphasizes curriculum and research programs that prepare graduates to support local, regional and national industry by analyzing large and complex datasets.\nVisit Department\nView Requirements\nCost and Aid\nQuick Facts\nLocations\nBrookings Main Campus\nCredits\n72 Credit Plan\nEst. Time to Completion\n3-5 years\nStart Term\nFall\nIs it for you?\nThis program will be a good fit if you:\nHave an undergraduate or master's degree in mathematics, statistics or related field.\nHave strong problem-solving and quantitative skills.\nAre able to grasp the essence of complex situations.\nHave good communication skills.\nWant your quantitative skills to have an impact.\nJob Outlook\nBack to top\nCareer Opportunities\nExplore possible career opportunities with this degree:\nData scientist\nPredictive analyst\nStatistician\nFinancial or business analyst\nRisk analyst\nProfessor\nResearcher\nReady to take the next step?\nContact Our Department\nRoss Abraham\nVisit Department\n605-688-4382\nHelpful Resources\nProgram Requirements\nGraduate Mathematics and Statistics Programs\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nTuition and Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply Now\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate School\nYou may also be interested in...\nArtificial Intelligence Engineering (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nComputational Science and Statistics (Ph.D.) \u2013 Mathematics Specialization\nGraduate\nComputational Science and Statistics (Ph.D.) \u2013 Statistics Specialization\nGraduate\nData Science (M.S.)\nGraduate\nEconomics (M.S.)\nGraduate\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info